[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi everyone! Congrats on completing the port! We are planning to implement our new project (A follow-up for Amaryllis) with Iris-Lean. I wanted to ask whether there are any plans currently for supporting ordered resource algebras (from MoSeL)? They are not in main Iris, but all the distributional probabilistic logics (including Lilac, Bluebell and Amaryllis) rely on them.</p>",
        "id": 619542299,
        "sender_full_name": "Janine Lohse",
        "timestamp": 1787836951
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think this would be possible and I have heard from two separate people in the probabilistic space asking about this feature. </p>\n<p>If I recall correctly from our conversation, this amounts to making ≼ and ≼{n} fields of CMRA, right?</p>",
        "id": 619544337,
        "sender_full_name": "Markus de Medeiros",
        "timestamp": 1787837408
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Nice! Yes, this is true. MoSeLs ORAs are also made and used to model non-affine logics, so for porting them as-is one would also need something like an affiness typeclass there.</p>",
        "id": 619545443,
        "sender_full_name": "Janine Lohse",
        "timestamp": 1787837637
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Great! I think this should be a relatively straightforward and backwards compatible so it's worth a try. Please make an issue, I can work on this but probably not in the next 3 weeks or so.</p>",
        "id": 619548403,
        "sender_full_name": "Markus de Medeiros",
        "timestamp": 1787838335
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If we agree on what the typeclass structure should be in the end, I could also make a draft :)</p>",
        "id": 619549003,
        "sender_full_name": "Janine Lohse",
        "timestamp": 1787838473
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh sure. The bulk of a prototype could be done as follows: first move <code>Included</code> and <code>IncludedN</code> into <code>CMRA</code>, and update all CMRA instances to use the new class. This will establish if the generalization is possible: I _think_ that the algebras we define generalize cleanly to ORAs but some proofs will need to be changed. This first prototype would answer the question as to if this is possible. </p>\n<p>In the final version I'd like to separating the monolithic CMRA class into a small <code>extends</code> family for <code>pcore</code> + laws, <code>op</code> + laws, <code>valid &amp; validN</code> + laws (with <code>CMRA</code> extending them all and adding the <code>extend</code> field). That would let you integrate a general lawful order into this hierarchy cleanly, and also provide a smart constructor for the old extension order. But separating the classes and adding extension should be done as two separate features, and both only after we know how the library generalizes to ORAs</p>",
        "id": 619557776,
        "sender_full_name": "Markus de Medeiros",
        "timestamp": 1787840376
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I have some probabilistic iris logics, I'll see what I can easily release separately.</p>",
        "id": 619562858,
        "sender_full_name": "Bas Spitters",
        "timestamp": 1787841475
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>@Markus You mean something like that?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">OFE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">├─</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Op</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">op</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">op_ne</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">assoc</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">comm</span><span class=\"w\">                          </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">laws</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">about</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">op</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">alone</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">├─</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PCore</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pcore</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pcore_ne</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pcore_idem</span><span class=\"w\">                      </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">laws</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">about</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pcore</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">alone</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">├─</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Valid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Valid</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ValidN</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">validN_ne</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">valid_iff_validN</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">validN_succ</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">└─</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">OrderN</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">OrderN</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Order</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">order_iff_orderN</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">orderN_succ</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">orderN_trans</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dist_orderN</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"general lawful order\"</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">RABase</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">extends</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">OFE</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Op</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PCore</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Valid</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">...</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"n\">mixed</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">laws</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">every</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">RA</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">like</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">thing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">has</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                                             </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">validN_op_left</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pcore_op_left</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">…</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">CMRA</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"kn\">extends</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">RABase</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\">                  </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pcore_op_mono</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">extend</span><span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">extension</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">order</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">specific</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">ORA</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kn\">extends</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">RABase</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">OrderN</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">orderN_op</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">validN_orderN</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pcore_monoN</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ora</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">extend</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">…</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Unital</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">extends</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">RABase</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\">                  </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">unit</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">unit_valid</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">unit_left_id</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pcore_unit</span>\n<span class=\"n\">UCMRA</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kn\">extends</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CMRA</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unital</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span>\n<span class=\"n\">UORA</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"kn\">extends</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ORA</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Unital</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">...</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 619562998,
        "sender_full_name": "Janine Lohse",
        "timestamp": 1787841511
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>We could then have for backwards-compatiblity </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">reducible</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ORA</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ofCMRA</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CMRA</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ORA</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ExtOrd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">UCMRA</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">UORA</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ExtOrd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">UORA</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ofCMRA</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">abbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">UPred</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">UCMRA</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">OUPred</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ExtOrd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 619569258,
        "sender_full_name": "Janine Lohse",
        "timestamp": 1787842870
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I assume the top diagram means <code>Op α extends OFE α</code>, <code>PCore α extends OFE α</code> etc. If the first prototype I described is possible and the library generalizes cleanly (every CMRA that takes a CMRA as an input can use the OrderN laws instead) we could essentially use the old hierarchy but with everything parametric on the order:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CMRA</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">extends</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">OFE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Op</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PCore</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Valid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">OrderN</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">...</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">-- the *mixed* laws + orderN_op, validN_orderN, pcore_monoN, ora-extend, …</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">OldCMRA</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">extends</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Op</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PCore</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Valid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- + Mixed laws</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">withExtensionOrder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">OldCMRA</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CMRA</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">...</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- Smart constructor, with proofs that an abstract extension order is an ORA</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">UCMRA</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kn\">extends</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CMRA</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- units and whatnot</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>On the other hand, if some constructions require their inputs be \"CMRA's with the extension order in particular\" we might use a hierarchy closer to yours. But there are a few ways to do that and we'd need to see what that requirement looks like first. </p>\n<p>Based on the proofs I've done myself I'm optimistic that a clean generalization is possible, but without a prototype I'm not certain. You know more about ORA's, what do you think?</p>",
        "id": 619569273,
        "sender_full_name": "Markus de Medeiros",
        "timestamp": 1787842874
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm a bit confused by your proposal, the mixed cmra laws are here not included in OldCMRA?</p>",
        "id": 619572596,
        "sender_full_name": "Janine Lohse",
        "timestamp": 1787843580
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah. Or they can be hypotheses on <code>withExtensionOrder</code>. Though I see now that I copy-pasted <code>OrderN</code> when I should not have.</p>",
        "id": 619573174,
        "sender_full_name": "Markus de Medeiros",
        "timestamp": 1787843709
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In fact it might even better as a structure rather than a class... anyways again there are a few ways to do this but it depends mostly on if the whole library can be generalized or not.</p>\n<p>Edit: Another way:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">RABase</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">extends</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">OFE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Op</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PCore</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Valid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- Mixed laws</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CMRA</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">extends</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">RABase</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">OrderN</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- + Mixed Order laws</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">RABase</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IncExt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- The extension order</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">RABase</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IncExtN</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- The indexed extension order</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">withExtensionOrder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">RABase</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CMRA</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- Smart constructor</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">UCMRA</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kn\">extends</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CMRA</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- units and whatnot</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 619573698,
        "sender_full_name": "Markus de Medeiros",
        "timestamp": 1787843816
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I expect it to generalize, but if anything specifically requires the extension order, there could just be a typeclass for it like for affiness I guess?</p>",
        "id": 619574456,
        "sender_full_name": "Janine Lohse",
        "timestamp": 1787843989
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah. The absolute cheapest way would be something like </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CMRA</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsExtensionOrder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"n\">inc_extension_iff</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≼</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span>\n<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"n\">incN_extension_iff</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≼</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≡</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"bp\">≡</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>And then rewrite by these theorems where needed</p>",
        "id": 619575801,
        "sender_full_name": "Markus de Medeiros",
        "timestamp": 1787844294
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>But also--if a failure to generalize depends on a property of the extension order rather than the full definition itself (akin more to affine-ness, which is a property rather than equality of two definitions) we could do this differently.</p>",
        "id": 619576714,
        "sender_full_name": "Markus de Medeiros",
        "timestamp": 1787844511
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That sounds good <span aria-label=\"+1\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f44d\" role=\"img\" title=\"+1\">:+1:</span> I guess I'll then first give it a try without the extension order typeclass, and see how it works?</p>",
        "id": 619578097,
        "sender_full_name": "Janine Lohse",
        "timestamp": 1787844790
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Another thing I noticed: one might also want a nice way to define a unital cmra with extension order</p>",
        "id": 619582040,
        "sender_full_name": "Janine Lohse",
        "timestamp": 1787845697
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This sounds interesting, but I am not familiar with ordered resource algebras in Rocq, so I have some more basic questions: How do the Rocq mechanizations handle ordered resource algebras? Are they already integrated into Iris Rocq, but missing in Iris Lean? Or is there some library that is missing in Lean? Or do they use a fork of Iris?</p>",
        "id": 619615558,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Sammler",
        "timestamp": 1787854093
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>There is a mechanization in Rocq <a href=\"https://github.com/mansky1/ora/tree/main\">here</a></p>",
        "id": 619650680,
        "sender_full_name": "Markus de Medeiros",
        "timestamp": 1787864447
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, they all use forks or add ORAs on top in their development</p>",
        "id": 619740151,
        "sender_full_name": "Janine Lohse",
        "timestamp": 1787906446
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Adding it as a library would require duplicating a lot of infrastructure, so what Markus suggested would be a much nicer and still backwards-compatible way, but it would mean Iris-Lean deviates from Iris-Rocq</p>",
        "id": 619740948,
        "sender_full_name": "Janine Lohse",
        "timestamp": 1787906708
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That makes sense <span aria-label=\"+1\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f44d\" role=\"img\" title=\"+1\">:+1:</span> Have you discussed such a change with the Iris Rocq maintainers? Would they be interested in adding support for ORAs directly in Iris Rocq?</p>",
        "id": 619777660,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Sammler",
        "timestamp": 1787918101
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>According to Robbert this breaks basic updates, which sounds like more of a problem</p>",
        "id": 619787374,
        "sender_full_name": "Markus de Medeiros",
        "timestamp": 1787920885
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I guess you would need an affiness side condition for them?</p>",
        "id": 619787992,
        "sender_full_name": "Janine Lohse",
        "timestamp": 1787921073
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The classical way to use ORAs is to strenghten the order and build non-affine logics, but all the distributional probabilistic logics weaken the order instead. (Amaryllis has updates + ORAs, but the ORA version we use is affine-only)</p>",
        "id": 619788554,
        "sender_full_name": "Janine Lohse",
        "timestamp": 1787921233
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Interesting. It sounds like the abstraction you might need is <code>IsExtensionOrder</code> above but with only one direction of the Iff?</p>",
        "id": 619790562,
        "sender_full_name": "Markus de Medeiros",
        "timestamp": 1787921774
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes. This boils down to x &lt;= x * y, which is exactly the affiness axiom</p>",
        "id": 619791232,
        "sender_full_name": "Janine Lohse",
        "timestamp": 1787921943
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah, nice! We'll have to see what the prototype looks like, but I could imagine this still being the kind of generalization that is feasible to add to Iris-Lean without the same difficulties as it would in Iris-Rocq. </p>\n<p>By the way, just to say it outright: inclusion of any feature that deviates from Iris-Rocq is not a foregone conclusion (preserving forwards-compatibility with the Rocq version means that such changes can not be made lightly). But this idea seems promising to me, and it also sounds like it will not block your research in any case :)</p>",
        "id": 619796088,
        "sender_full_name": "Markus de Medeiros",
        "timestamp": 1787923160
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Sure. If it doesn't end up upstream, its going to live in my fork :)</p>",
        "id": 619796293,
        "sender_full_name": "Janine Lohse",
        "timestamp": 1787923211
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I drafted a PR for this: <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/iris-lean/pull/688\">https://github.com/leanprover-community/iris-lean/pull/688</a></p>",
        "id": 620712194,
        "sender_full_name": "Janine Lohse",
        "timestamp": 1788278267
    }
]